commit 52b40fdc88abef6d88a67a9a5067e8429eb95d83

C03: the preference acknowledgement names the person's taste and never the assistant's own tastes, offers or questions (MEMORY1503)

MEMORY1501 measured that «Me gusta tomar café.» was already a social turn with zero operations, but the model invented its own tastes («Me encanta el café…», «¡A mí también!») and offers («¿Quieres un té…?»). The first-person preference reader moves to `effect_intent.first_person_preference` (shared by `_personal_checkin_statement`) and the social turn gets a presentation shape, `preference_ack`: the prompt asks for one short sentence acknowledging and naming the person's preference, and the contract rejects questions, more than two sentences, answers that do not name the thing, the assistant's own tastes («me encanta», «a mí también», «prefiero», «my favourite»…), offers to prepare, serve or bring anything, and claims of having saved or remembered it. Payload {response_language, preference, thing}; 128-token group like reassurance_ack.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


